# Test: an operator can type `show bgp update-delay` and read the hold out of it
# Spec: spec-bgp-update-delay (closed 2026-09-11)
# accept-only: the registered native fixture enforces this scenario's behavioral contract
#
# VALIDATES: the command is reachable from the entry point a person's keystrokes
#            take, and its answer carries the fields the documentation tells them
#            to read. The daemon is configured with two peers that never answer
#            and `max-delay 300`, so it is still holding when the command runs.
#
# PREVENTS:  the defect this file was written for. The command node was declared
#            in a module whose name ends -api, BuildCommandTree walks -cmd
#            modules alone, so no CLI path existed. Both dispatchers took their
#            "no path" branch and CONTINUED IN SILENCE while three documentation
#            pages told an operator to run it. The handler had unit tests and
#            they all passed: they called the handler directly, which is the half
#            that worked.
#
# The companion is TestShowBgpUpdateDelayIsRegistered
# (internal/component/bgp/plugins/cmd/peer/update_delay_registration_test.go),
# which asserts the PATH exists in the YANG command tree. This file asserts a
# daemon answers it. Neither one alone would have caught the defect: the tree
# test cannot see a broken handler, and this one cannot run without a daemon.
#
# The timeout is DECLARED because this file starts a daemon and launches `ze`
# twice, which a cold run or a loaded host can take past the runner's derived
# bound while every assertion still holds.
option=timeout:value=60s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze-test fixture ui/bgp-update-delay
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK
